   ├─ quota: 3 left (apply spends 1)
   ├─ picks (1, in order)
   │  └─ 1. <sha> cont(wave): add swell height
   ├─ left behind on turtle/wave-report (2, not picked)
   │  ├─ <sha> feat(wave): add wave report
   │  └─ <sha> cont(wave): add tide window
   ├─ tracked edits (1) — will park, verify, and carry, unstaged
   │  └─ M src/wave.ts
   └─ carry will halt (1) — edits to files the new branch lacks
      ├─ src/wave.ts (added by <sha> feat(wave): add wave report, not picked)
      └─ fix: --pick the commit named, or commit or drop the edit first

run with --mode apply to execute
"
`;

exports[`git.branch.cutover given: [case70] a tracked edit to a file a left-behind commit adds when: [t2] apply, without the pick then: the carry halts, and says the new branch lacks the file 1`] = `
"🐢 hang tight...

🐚 git.branch.cutover begin --mode apply
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: halted: the carry of tracked edits conflicts
      ├─ into: turtle/wave-v2 (checked out, no upstream)
      ├─ picks (1, in order)
      │  └─ 1. <sha> → <sha> cont(wave): add swell height ✓
      ├─ tracked edits ✋ conflict on carry
      │  └─ files
      │     └─ src/wave.ts (the new branch lacks it; a commit not picked adds it. keep it, or rhx rmsafe it)
      ├─ safe: original tracked edits held at refs/worktree/cutover/tree
      ├─ stage: ✋ no stage grant, so rhx git.stage.add will refuse
      │  └─ ask your human: git.commit.uses set --quant N --push allow|block --stage allow
      └─ quota: the cutover unit is spent; abort refunds none

🥥 did you know?
   ├─ settle the files above, stage them, then continue — or undo the whole cutover; a file you delete stages the same way
   ├─ rhx git.stage.add <files>
   ├─ rhx git.branch.cutover continue
   └─ rhx git.branch.cutover abort
"
`;

exports[`git.branch.cutover given: [case72] a tracked edit saved while the apply runs when: [t1] the edit lands after the park, before the reset then: the cut backs out, and every edit stays in place 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.branch.cutover
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: tracked edits changed while the cutover ran; naught changed
      ├─ why: an edit was saved after the park, so a reset would lose it
      └─ fix: let the other editor finish, then rerun the same command
"
`;

exports[`git.branch.cutover given: [case76] a --from spelled as a remote-track ref or as HEAD when: [t0] --from origin/main then: it refuses, and points to @main 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.branch.cutover
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: --from names the branch origin holds; drop the origin/ prefix
      ├─ why: the cutover reads origin itself, after a fetch
      └─ fix: --from @main (or --from main)
"
`;

exports[`git.branch.cutover given: [case76] a --from spelled as a remote-track ref or as HEAD when: [t2] --from HEAD then: it refuses, and points to @tree 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.branch.cutover
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: --from HEAD is spelled --from @tree
      ├─ why: @tree stacks on this tree's HEAD, with every commit kept
      └─ fix: --from @tree
"
`;
